=== file: README.md ===
# Overnight Error Report

This is a deliberately gated scaffold, not an activated scheduled integration. The team has not supplied a timezone, log location, channel destination, or delivery approval policy. There is no schedule declaration and no channel send is performed.

## Current workflow contract

- `SetupGate` asks the workflow setup owner for the missing setup details, then returns them for operator configuration. That answer does not activate a schedule or delivery.
- `Main` is for a manually supplied batch only. Its caller must establish that the source was available and that redaction was completed and verified before passing evidence. A batch above 10,000 lines is sent to the on-call approver for assessment and is not analyzed.
- Unavailable logs produce an unavailable status without findings. Analysis errors or invalid structured output halt the workflow. The analyst has no tools and receives only the supplied evidence; PII masking is enabled as defense in depth.
- Every prepared report is presented to the on-call approver. The response and report are returned to the caller; no channel delivery is enabled, even if the reviewer approves.

## Required before production

The plan names `OvernightLogs`, `SanitizeAndChunk`, and `OnCallChannel` as stubs. Their operational configurations are intentionally not fabricated here: the source path and format are unknown, the deterministic sanitizer/chunker implementation is not provided, and the channel destination is unconfirmed. In particular, `SanitizeAndChunk` requires an operator-provided deterministic implementation. Until it exists and is tested, do not treat an input attestation as proof that arbitrary logs were sanitized.

Before enabling a scheduled path, configure a read-only log source, install and test a deterministic sanitizer that redacts secrets and personal data before model processing and enforces the 10,000-line bound, confirm chunking behavior, configure the destination, and define explicit per-report approval. Then update the workflow and add tests for configured reads, tool failures, and the single approved send. Never retry a channel send automatically.

The only model is the plan-specified `gpt-6-luna`; verify that it is available in the deployment's model registry before running.

## Checks

```text
weave check main.loom --no-env
weave test main.loom
weave eval main.loom --mock
```
